<metadata xml:lang="en"><Esri><CreaDate>20251010</CreaDate><CreaTime>06475100</CreaTime><ArcGISFormat>1.0</ArcGISFormat><SyncOnce>TRUE</SyncOnce><ModDate>20251010</ModDate><ModTime>7550000</ModTime><scaleRange><minScale>150000000</minScale><maxScale>5000</maxScale></scaleRange><ArcGISProfile>ItemDescription</ArcGISProfile></Esri><tool name="Madtool" displayname="MADk2" toolboxalias="" xmlns=""><arcToolboxHelpPath>c:\program files\arcgis\pro\Resources\Help\gp</arcToolboxHelpPath><parameters><param name="in_raster" displayname="Input Raster" type="Required" direction="Input" datatype="Raster Layer" expression="in_raster"/><param name="out_workspace" displayname="Output Workspace" type="Required" direction="Input" datatype="Workspace" expression="out_workspace"/><param name="window_radius" displayname="Search Window Radius (cells)" type="Required" direction="Input" datatype="Long" expression="window_radius"/><param name="lag_distance" displayname="Lag Distance (cells)" type="Required" direction="Input" datatype="String" expression="1 pixel | 2 pixels"/></parameters><summary>&lt;DIV STYLE="text-align:Left;"&gt;&lt;DIV&gt;&lt;DIV&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN STYLE="font-size:16pt"&gt;Simplified geostatistical aproach for surface roughness/ image texture analysis. Provide omnidirectional roughness and roughness anisotropy.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN STYLE="font-size:16pt"&gt;It returns 3 files: omnidirectional roughness (same units of input raster), roughness anisotropy strength (dimensionless, between 0 and 1, with 1 maximum anisotropy) and roughness anisotropy direction (geographical convention). For example, selecting a lag of 1 pixel and a search radius of 3 pixels these are the returned files.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN STYLE="font-size:16pt"&gt;RoughIsoc1k2_r3.tif&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN STYLE="font-size:16pt"&gt;RoughAnisoc1k2_r3.tif&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN STYLE="font-size:16pt"&gt;RoughAnisoDirc1k2_r3.tif&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN STYLE="font-size:16pt"&gt;For details see:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN STYLE="font-size:16pt"&gt;Trevisani, S., Teza, G., Guth, P., 2023. A simplified geostatistical approach for characterizing key aspects of short-range roughness. CATENA 223. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.catena.2023.106927&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN STYLE="font-size:16pt"&gt;https://zenodo.org/records/7716927&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN /&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;</summary><usage>&lt;DIV STYLE="text-align:Left;"&gt;&lt;DIV&gt;&lt;DIV&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN STYLE="font-size:16pt"&gt;Select the input raster (image/DEM), the radius of the search window (minimum 3 pixels) and the lag distance (1 or 2 pixels).&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN /&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;</usage></tool><dataIdInfo><idCitation><resTitle>MADk2</resTitle></idCitation><searchKeys><keyword>Surface roughness/image texture</keyword></searchKeys></dataIdInfo><distInfo><distributor><distorFormat><formatName>ArcToolbox Tool</formatName></distorFormat></distributor></distInfo><mdHrLv><ScopeCd value="005"/></mdHrLv><mdDateSt Sync="TRUE">20251010</mdDateSt></metadata>
